From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apex kernel <apex@kernel>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] uapi: sched: rename sched_param to __kernel_sched_param

Rename the UAPI struct sched_param to __kernel_sched_param to avoid
a conflict with bionic's sched_param in <sched.h>. This is needed for
AOSP ROM (LineageOS, etc.) compilation against the apex kernel headers.

The internal kernel code uses its own struct sched_param from
include/linux/sched.h (forward declaration), so the UAPI rename only
affects userspace-visible headers.

Based on LineageOS commit f0b1169abd007a6c3417270047297b942e727553
and SM6225-Android-Playground commit 2e2880a8513be97089a53fd5c2fdcb06891e2ac6.

Signed-off-by: apex kernel <apex@kernel>
---
 include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h b/include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/types.h>
 
-struct sched_param {
+struct __kernel_sched_param {
 	int sched_priority;
 };
 
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ struct sched_param {
  * This is needed because the original struct sched_param can not be
  * altered without introducing ABI issues with legacy applications
  * (e.g., in sched_getparam()).
- * However, the possibility of specifying more than just a priority for
+ * However, the possibility of specifying more than just a priority for
  * the tasks may be useful for a wide variety of application fields, e.g.,
  * multimedia, streaming, automation and control, and many others.
  * This variant (sched_attr) allows to define additional attributes to
